text:
DHS approved a $1.5B contract with the same company that provided security at Alligator Alcatraz to build and expand detention facilities in Arizona.

Local governments didn't find out about it until after the contract was awarded. These are your tax dollars being used for facilities that repeatedly commit human rights violations - and they're not giving us a say in the matter.

@AdelitaForAZ , @gregstantonaz and I are fighting back.

The @DemWomenCaucus and I are deeply disgusted by DHS and ICE’s failure to provide care for and account for miscarriages and pregnancy-related medical outcomes in detention centers.

@RepPettersen, @RepBeatty, and I led a letter condemning their actions.

They must be held accountable.

Everyone deserves accessible health care, and cuts from HR1 (Republicans’ Big Ugly budget Bill) are endangering Oregonians’ health care access and funding to places like CAP NW.

I will keep fighting until Oregonians have access to the care they need with the safety and dignity they deserve. 

@EqualityCaucus 
@HouseDemocrats
